{
  "info": {
    "name": "SafeIn5 — API (Auth · Signals · Uploads)",
    "description": "Passwordless signup + login (email OTP + magic link), signals, and chunked video upload.\n\nBase URL: {{baseUrl}} (default http://localhost:3000). Feature routes are under /api/v1.\n\nOTP FLOW: the OTP code and magic link are printed to the SERVER LOG (dev mailer), not returned in the response. Steps:\n1. Run 'Register' (or 'Request OTP').\n2. Copy the 6-digit code from the server log line: [DEV MAIL] OTP for <email>: NNNNNN\n3. Paste it into the collection variable 'otp' (or the Verify OTP request body).\n4. Run 'Verify OTP' — it auto-saves the accessToken into the 'accessToken' variable, so everything else just works.\n\nThe refresh token is an HttpOnly cookie; Postman's cookie jar handles it automatically for 'Refresh' and 'Logout'.\n\nUPLOADS (guided flow): run '1. Initiate', then click '2. Upload next part bytes' once per part. Initiate returns the signed URL for part 1; each PUT records the part and returns the NEXT part's URL (captured into nextUrl), and the last PUT auto-assembles and returns { completed }. Just keep clicking 2 until the console logs 'UPLOAD COMPLETED'. No confirm/complete needed. The bearer token is OPTIONAL: clear the collection 'accessToken' variable (or remove the request auth) to upload anonymously.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "sam@example.com" },
    { "key": "otp", "value": "" },
    { "key": "magicToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "signalId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "uploadId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "nextUrl", "value": "" },
    { "key": "nextPart", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness (healthz)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["healthz"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness (readyz)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/readyz", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["readyz"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register (signup)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Sam\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Rivera\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates the account (if new) and sends an OTP. Returns 204. Read the OTP from the server log, then run Verify OTP."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Request OTP (login)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/otp/request",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "otp", "request"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a fresh OTP to an existing account. Always 204 (no account enumeration)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.test('saved accessToken', () => pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "  }",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('verify failed: ' + pm.response.code, () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "otp", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the code (paste it into the 'otp' variable first). On 200, auto-saves accessToken and sets the refresh cookie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Request Magic Link",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/magic-link",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "magic-link"]
            },
            "description": "Emails (logs) a magic link. Copy the token at the end of the logged URL into the 'magicToken' variable, then run Verify Magic Link."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Magic Link",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken); }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/magic/{{magicToken}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "magic", "{{magicToken}}"]
            },
            "description": "Consumes the magic-link token. On 200, saves accessToken and sets the refresh cookie."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh (cookie)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken); }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Issues a new access token from the refresh cookie (set at login). Postman sends the cookie automatically."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Clears the refresh cookie. Returns 204."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Me",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Requires a valid access token (auto-filled from Verify OTP). Returns { id, email, firstName, lastName, emailVerified, role, tenant }."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Signals",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create signal",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('signalId', json.id); }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"classification\": \"needs_attention_now\",\n  \"bodyText\": \"Exposed edge on level 2, no barrier\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a signal for the current user. classification: good_practice | be_aware | needs_attention_now. Add \"anonymous\": true to hide the author. Saves the new id into 'signalId'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create anonymous signal",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"classification\": \"be_aware\",\n  \"bodyText\": \"Someone bypassing the lockout\",\n  \"anonymous\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals"]
            },
            "description": "Anonymous report: the response and every feed/get returns author: null and isAnonymous: true."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Feed",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/feed?limit=50",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "feed"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "50" }]
            },
            "description": "All signals, newest first (default 50, max 100)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "My signals",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals/mine",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals", "mine"]
            },
            "description": "The current user's own signals, newest first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get signal by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals/{{signalId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals", "{{signalId}}"]
            },
            "description": "One signal by id (auto-filled from Create signal)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Acknowledge (supervisor)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals/{{signalId}}/acknowledge",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals", "{{signalId}}", "acknowledge"]
            },
            "description": "Supervisor only (403 for a worker). Role is on the tenant membership; make a supervisor in psql:\nUPDATE user_tenant_membership m SET role='supervisor' FROM app_user u WHERE u.id=m.user_id AND u.email='boss@example.com';\nthen log that user in so the token's role is supervisor. Only signals in the caller's own tenant are visible (cross-tenant -> 404). open -> acknowledged (idempotent)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Close (supervisor)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"closeNote\": \"Barrier reinstated, area cleared\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/signals/{{signalId}}/close",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "signals", "{{signalId}}", "close"]
            },
            "description": "Supervisor only, note required. open/acknowledged -> closed; closing again -> 409."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Feed — open only",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/feed?status=open",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "feed"],
              "query": [{ "key": "status", "value": "open" }]
            },
            "description": "Supervisor 'needs response' list: only open signals."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Uploads (chunked, guided)",
      "description": "GUIDED FLOW. Run '1. Initiate', then click '2. Upload next part bytes' once per part. Each upload records the part and captures the NEXT part's signed URL (into nextUrl/nextPart), so just keep clicking 2 until the console logs 'UPLOAD COMPLETED' (the last part auto-assembles). No confirm/complete needed. The bearer token is OPTIONAL (clear the 'accessToken' variable, or remove the request auth, to upload anonymously).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Initiate upload",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadId', j.id);",
                  "  if (j.next) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('nextUrl', j.next.uploadUrl);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('nextPart', j.next.partNumber);",
                  "  }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"filename\": \"clip.mp4\",\n  \"mimeType\": \"video/mp4\",\n  \"totalParts\": 3\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/initiate",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "uploads", "initiate"]
            },
            "description": "Starts a 3-part upload. Optionally add \"totalBytes\" and a whole-file \"checksum\" (sha256 hex) for end-to-end verification. Saves 'uploadId' and the FIRST part's signed URL (into 'nextUrl'/'nextPart')."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Upload next part bytes (advances to the next URL)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (j.completed) {",
                  "    console.log('UPLOAD COMPLETED:', JSON.stringify(j.completed));",
                  "  } else if (j.next) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('nextUrl', j.next.uploadUrl);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('nextPart', j.next.partNumber);",
                  "    console.log('Next part:', j.next.partNumber, 'missing:', JSON.stringify(j.missingParts));",
                  "  }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/octet-stream" }],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "part-bytes-sample-" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{nextUrl}}" },
            "description": "PUT the raw part bytes to the signed URL captured from the previous step ('nextUrl'). The response records the part and returns { next } (captured into 'nextUrl'/'nextPart') OR { completed } on the LAST part (auto-assembles + deletes temp parts). Just click this once per part until the console logs 'UPLOAD COMPLETED'. Body is sample text; for a real video switch Body to 'binary' and pick a file chunk (a different one per part)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Status (optional)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/{{uploadId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "uploads", "{{uploadId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Current status: { status, receivedCount, receivedParts, missingParts, ... }."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Abort a pending upload (optional)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/{{uploadId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "uploads", "{{uploadId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Discards a still-pending upload and its temp parts. 200 -> { status: 'aborted' } (409 if already completed)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
